# Fabro execute workflow — operating guide

The dark-factory loop lives in `.fabro/workflows/execute/`. Run it for one module at a time. Module is **required** on every run (no default).

## Launch

```bash
fabro run .fabro/workflows/execute/workflow.toml -I module=<domain-folder>
fabro run .fabro/workflows/execute/workflow.toml -I module=domains-catalog
fabro run .fabro/workflows/execute/workflow.toml -I module=src-root
```

## Stages (simplified graph)

`scope → clarify_prep → clarify [gate] → plan → verification [gate] → setup → developer (codex) → verify → retro`

No separate assess, tester, e2e, screenshot, or preview stages.

## Human gates (fail-closed, 24h timeout)

| Gate | Buttons | Timeout default |
|------|---------|-----------------|
| **clarify** | [A]/[B]/[C] module-specific (see prep summary) · [F] Custom · [R] Re-scope | → `plan` (A) |
| **verification** | [A] Approve & build · [B] Plan only · [I] Iterate · [X] Abort | → `retro` (plan only — **never auto-builds**) |

## Verify stage

`node scripts/fabro-verify.mjs` — module-scoped typecheck + ESLint + module unit tests, then **husky pre-commit parity** (architecture, docs, full unit tests, production build). Commit-ready handoff when exit 0.

**Many failures in verify loops:** developer uses `.local/quality-backlog.md` (`npm run qualitygate:capture`) — one fix per step, rescan every 5; see `.agents/execute/partials/quality-backlog.md`.

**Fix loops:** verify fails → developer (codex) retries up to **3 times** (`max_visits=4`). After that → retro anyway (**ship anyway** — does not block PR).

## Artifacts

`CLARIFY.md`, `DECISIONS.md`, `PLAN.md`, `STRUCTURE.md` (catalog/src-root), `RETRO.md`. Do **not** commit `CLARIFY.md`/`DECISIONS.md` — stale copies poison Docker clones.

`RETRO.md` must be **evidence-based** (git diff verified) — never trust developer handoff summaries alone.

## Merge a successful run

```bash
fabro pr create <run-id>
```

